{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Long-Context Evaluation \u2014 NIAH, RULER, LongBench, MRCR Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: a custom NIAH for your domain"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "See `code/main.py`. The skeleton:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def build_haystack(filler_text, needle, depth_ratio, total_tokens):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if not (0.0 <= depth_ratio <= 1.0):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        raise ValueError(f\"depth_ratio must be in [0, 1], got {depth_ratio}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if total_tokens <= 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        raise ValueError(f\"total_tokens must be positive, got {total_tokens}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    filler_tokens = tokenize(filler_text)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    needle_tokens = tokenize(needle)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if not filler_tokens:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        raise ValueError(\"filler_text produced no tokens\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    # Repeat filler until long enough to fill the haystack body."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    body_len = max(total_tokens - len(needle_tokens), 0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    while len(filler_tokens) < body_len:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        filler_tokens = filler_tokens + filler_tokens"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    filler_tokens = filler_tokens[:body_len]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    insert_at = min(int(body_len * depth_ratio), body_len)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    haystack = filler_tokens[:insert_at] + needle_tokens + filler_tokens[insert_at:]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return \" \".join(haystack)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def score_niah(model, haystack, question, expected):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    answer = model.complete(f\"Context: {haystack}\\nQ: {question}\\nA:\", max_tokens=50)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return 1 if expected.lower() in answer.lower() else 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Sweep `depth_ratio` \u2208 {0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1.0} \u00d7 `total_tokens` \u2208 {1k, 4k, 16k, 64k}. Plot the heatmap. That is the NIAH card for your target model."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: a multi-needle variant"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def build_multi_needle(filler, needles, total_tokens):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    depths = [0.1, 0.4, 0.7]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    chunks = [filler[:int(total_tokens * 0.1)]]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for depth, needle in zip(depths, needles):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        chunks.append(needle)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        next_chunk = filler[int(total_tokens * depth): int(total_tokens * (depth + 0.3))]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        chunks.append(next_chunk)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return \" \".join(chunks)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Questions like \"What are the three magic words?\" require retrieving all three. Single-needle success does not predict multi-needle success."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: multi-hop variable tracing (RULER-style)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "haystack = \"\"\"X1 = 42. ... (filler) ... X2 = X1 + 10. ... (filler) ... X3 = X2 * 2.\"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "question = \"What is X3?\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The answer requires chaining three assignments. Frontier models at 128k often drop to 50-70% accuracy here."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: LongBench v2 on your stack"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from datasets import load_dataset"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "longbench = load_dataset(\"THUDM/LongBench-v2\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def eval_model_on_longbench(model, subset=\"single-doc-qa\"):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    tasks = [x for x in longbench[\"test\"] if x[\"task\"] == subset]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    correct = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for x in tasks:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        answer = model.complete(x[\"context\"] + \"\\n\\nQ: \" + x[\"question\"], max_tokens=20)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if normalize(answer) == normalize(x[\"answer\"]):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            correct += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return correct / len(tasks)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Report per-category accuracy. Aggregate scores hide big task-level differences."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Build a NIAH with 3 depths (0.25, 0.5, 0.75) \u00d7 3 lengths (1k, 4k, 16k). Run on any model. Plot pass rate as a 3\u00d73 heatmap.\n2. **Medium.** Add a 3-needle variant. Measure retrieval of all 3 at each length. Compare to single-needle pass rate at the same length.\n3. **Hard.** Construct a variable-tracing task (X1 \u2192 X2 \u2192 X3, with 3 hops) embedded in 64k of filler. Measure accuracy across 3 frontier models. Report effective reasoning length per model."
      ]
    }
